{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/110761-powerlevel-of-mummies-relative-to-other-supernaturals","id":110761,"title":"Powerlevel of Mummies relative to other Supernaturals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-11T06:51:43-07:00","id":110761,"title":"Powerlevel of Mummies relative to other Supernaturals","content":"Mummies seem to be the royalty of the WOD, the 1% as it where, and there are 3rd level Invocation powers that make them almost godlike. However, I do find that once their access to the higher powers is severed (after about 40 days, assuming that they had access in the first place), then their powers become more modest. Add to the fact that they are most powerful in their first few weeks, and then see a decline in their ability to fuel attributes.<br /> <br /> Add to the fact that they are out of commission for long stretches so that would also hamper their ability to be movers and shakers.<br /> <br /> How do others find the power of mummies relative to other citizens of the World of Darkness?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T09:18:02-07:00","id":110835,"title":"","content":"While some of those Tier 3 Utterances are extremely powerful they are often never going to get used.<br /> <br /> When was the last time you needed to flatten a city for example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T10:46:36-07:00","id":110908,"title":"","content":"In my mixed game so far, the mummy has been the bullet shield. his wife (a demon) knows full well she can die for good and he can't, as do their team mates.. so typically, if its a dangerous encounter, the Mummy goes in first. Oddly, the tier 3 powers weren't nearly as OP as raising your stats to 8 each for peanuts, and smearing everyon's faces clean off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T11:12:13-07:00","id":110934,"title":"","content":"Personally, I find Mummy to be in a bit of an odd situation when it comes to comparing it to the other major Supernatural splats at the moment. <br /> <br /> I think its because were are in the middle of an &quot;edition change&quot; for NWoD. Everything since God Machine has been getting a facelift that changes the idea of the comparative &quot;levels&quot; of each supernatural to one another. <br /> <br /> For example, in NWoD 1.0 Vampires were hands down the weakest Major splat. Their powers were the least versatile and lacked the sheer power of a lot of later splats. Their weaknesses were easily available (fire and sunlight) and their supernatural resource (blood) was one of the hardest to get and easiest for other supernaturals to screw with.<br /> <br /> Strix has changed some of that. The base Vampire template is now much, much stronger and sunlight is not such an issue anymore. Blood is still as much of a problem as ever, but that's part of Vampires theme, so I don't have an issue with that. Disciplines have also got a shot in the arm and are now comparable to Changeling and Promethean powers I feel. <br /> <br /> One thing that Mummy's do well is absorb damage, as their healing is the best of any Major splat at current. I suspect they will be usurped from this position by the 2.0 edition of Werewolf, but that's just a hunch I have. <br /> <br /> I'd be inclined to put them on about the same level as Sin-Eaters, their powers are a little less focused but otherwise I think the two are quite equal in ability. Demons are in about the same category I think, but that's dependent on XP and what the ST is doing with the rules for their powers.<br /> <br /> @ Cleverest of Things - A Crossover game with a Mummy married to a Demon? I want to hear more of this craziness. What are the other players playing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T11:23:14-07:00","id":110943,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/110761-powerlevel-of-mummies-relative-to-other-supernaturals?p=110835#post110835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While some of those Tier 3 Utterances are extremely powerful they are often never going to get used.<br /> <br /> When was the last time you needed to flatten a city for example?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Good point! That would be extremely unsubtle. Especially since the default setting will be Washington D.C. I do not see how the &quot;powers that be&quot; will be able to pull meteor storms out of the skies without CNN and every other news network going nuts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T17:22:36-07:00","id":111132,"title":"","content":"Tier 3 Utterances are ludicrously strong, but even Tier 1 and Tier 2 powers are, in my experience, pretty fantastic. Chthonic Dominion, for example, has a Tier 2 Utterance that lets you give a Ghost an open-ended command that it must attempt to follow for the rest of its existence. Pretty much all my non-Mummy experience has been with Changelings, but I can't think of many Contracts that give you such an automatic win as that. It's on par with the high level Vainglory Clauses, at the very least. The Secrets Ripped From Stars (or something along those lines) at Tier 2 calls down a meteor strike with a dice pool that certainly eclipses that of any offensive Clause that I know of. And Affinities often grant permanent powers that are stronger than most low-level Clauses as well. So, I certainly put Mummies at a higher level than Changelings.<br /> <br /> Then there's the existence of Sybaris. The first ever fight a Mummy will be involved in will likely end promptly due to every mortal fleeing more than any other outcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T19:34:36-07:00","id":111174,"title":"","content":"Mummy are the stompiest default beginning characters. And they aren't really even starting characters. Mummies might start off being weaker then they were a Sothic Turn ago due to memory loss. All Mummies don't have stats of starting characters because the more active they are the more exp they build and the more they I guess retain. So even though you could be the same age some mummies might actually have a bunch more utterances and traits exceeding 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T19:42:17-07:00","id":111181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/110761-powerlevel-of-mummies-relative-to-other-supernaturals?p=110835#post110835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While some of those Tier 3 Utterances are extremely powerful they are often never going to get used.<br /> <br /> When was the last time you needed to flatten a city for example?</div> </div> </div> </div>You never <i>need </i> to flatten a city.<br /> <br /> You need to <i>make</i> a reason to do so. Which isn't hard, really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T19:50:10-07:00","id":111186,"title":"","content":"When do you normally have the opportunity to flatten a city outside of Mummy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T04:57:22-07:00","id":111395,"title":"","content":"I've been listening to DaveB's <i>Mummy </i>podcast and I can't help but pull my hair out at their hesitance to use high-tier utterances.<br /> <br /> In one instance they were wondering if they should bust out a Mummy's cult members from prison, and they don't want to just smash their way through the wall! They were like, Sekhem 8 or 7 at the time! Maybe I would just be a GM's nightmare in a <i>Mummy</i> game but when you can hurl meteors and breathe fire there's a certain point where you aren't going to care about mundane consequences. Even in other games it's the same case. High Blood Potency Vampires don't play by the rules - they make them.<br /> <br /> That's part of the fun with <i>Mummy</i>: you go from not caring at all about the means to your ends, to falling through the Descent, and now suddenly you start caring about the 'masquerade' a lot more. Part of the fun, as a player, is thinking, &quot;Ah, remember when we could just run around like balrogs? Those were the days&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T05:31:14-07:00","id":111411,"title":"","content":"Reseru, I feel your pain about players being conservative with their powers. My players are currently at Sekhem 9, and I'm setting up scenarios where they can flex their muscles so to speak, but they are all very prudent in their approach. I need to find a way to make them consider a different mindset when playing mummy. It's in the early moments of the chronicle that they should be steamrolling everyone, caution be damned! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Which of course makes springing the eventual consequences on them when they're lower on the Sekhem scale all the more sweet.<br /> <br /> And do feel free to share the DaveB Mummy podcast!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">Malkavian Madness Forum</a> - Your pbp fix. Be it nWoD, cWoD, CoC, D&amp;D or something else entirely, come over here and get your game on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/348-infernalgoose","name":"InfernalGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T16:42:30-07:00","id":111820,"title":"","content":"Arisen relative power levels fluctuate for obvious reasons, but can be stabilized at a relatively high level in certain circumstances. <br /> <br /> 1. Guildhalls gives us the means to sustain access to 2nd and 3rd tier utterances through a talisman. <br /> 2. It is possible to retain full access to all utterance tiers while in one's tomb through the purchase of a single affinity available at character creation. <br /> 3. Another affinity allows for the storage of high-level utterances for later use. <br /> 4. Several powers allow for maximum stat boosts for very little cost, regardless of Sekhem level. <br /> 4. Apotheosis allows access to an essentially permanently elevated power level, save for access to the upper tiers of utterances. At that point, you are awake most of the time, can raise all of your abilities to superhuman levels, and have the capacity to accrue a ridiculous number of affinities and support them, perhaps indefinitely. <br /> <br /> All of this ignores the rapid healing, resistance to damage, and the built-in mechanics that allow, and even encourage, the use of a cult and a potential mob of supernatural retainers as an extension of the Arisen character, even if it happens to be sleeping at the time.<br /> <br /> And killing them is harder than with any other creature in the nWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2096-willywonka","name":"willywonka","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}